<title>SPAIN: Spanish retail sales rose 3.43 y/y in January.</title>
<headline>Spanish retail sales rose 3.43 y/y in January.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish retail sales data for January 1997 showed a 3.43 rise from December, and a 16.78 percent fall versus the same month one year ago, National Statistics Institute INE said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>INE gave the following breakdown:</p>
<p>				   VS DEC 96	VS JAN 96</p>
<p> General index		-16.78 pct	3.43 pct</p>
<p> Food			   -23.01 pct	1.13 pct</p>
<p> Personal goods		 1.27 pct	6.42 pct</p>
<p> Household goods	    -15.23 pct	0.73 pct</p>
<p> Other consumer goods     -20.99 pct	8.03 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Other consumer goods include toys and personal computers</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
